 is professional and of course  your summary your and then what do you  have to offer the company and again when  I put out resumes and I haven't done a  resume in a while you go in there and  you can take this and reorganize this so  if the company is looking for something  specific you might put the experiences  specific to that company you might even  take experience if you have like a long  job history like I do I've gone into a  lot of different things you might leave  out those companies or those experiences  that had nothing to do with data science  because it just becomes overwhelming  resume should only take about 30 seconds  to glance over maybe a minute tops  because after that point you've lost the  person's interest and if they want to  dig deeper they now have links they have  your website they have LinkedIn and they  can now take this and they come back to  it they go okay let's look at this  person a little closer so a quick  overview this is your cell sheet selling  you to the company so always tie it to  the company so that you have that what  am I gonna give this company what are  they gonna get from me we've covered a  lot on data science engineer in general  and we've gone over a basic resume  remember keep it simple short and direct  that is so important with that resume  thank you for joining us with data  science engineer salary skills and  resume again my name is Richard Kirchner  with the simply learned team that's wwm  play learn comm come visit our website  to learn more about what we have to  offer in the education and getting you  certified if you have  questions you can also post them down  below in the YouTube video we do have  people monitoring this channel hi there  if you like this video subscribe to the  simple learn YouTube channel and click  here to watch similar videos to nerd up  and get certified click here
 

